Z||000000||Adrift||10-04-2001||12:27 PM||||I bought a pair of two way- 6 1/2" speakers.  Here is my question: I don't have enough $$$ for door pods, unless I want to fabricate them myself. What are the requirements for mounting speakers in the door? Does there have to be any room between the back of the speaker and it's inclosure? i know air space is needed for woofers, but what about 6 1/2's? If I construct a pod myself, what should I take into consideration?<BR>Thanks+<BR>Adrift||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-04-2001||12:51 PM||||My problem with the door panel speakers is that your knees don't need to hear the music.  I'd put them in the dash if they fit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||heavyhorse||10-04-2001||01:22 PM||||How handy are you?  I took a day off work and completely disassembled my dash.  I was able to get 6x9 triaxials in there with some mods, so if you want to mount yours in the dash instead of the doors, i can give you more details.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroRacer||10-04-2001||05:16 PM||||I'd like more details||||reg||1
Z||000004||86seyellow||10-04-2001||08:54 PM||||I put 6x9s in the rear of the car. speaker boxes behind the seats angled up. they dont block anyhting since the seats are so high anywya and the cops cant see them also because I have black tint on every window.<P>Please make sure to vote in the discussion area.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1_copy1.jpg">    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_01.jpg">  <P>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-04-2001||10:17 PM||||i've gotten to where i hesitate to post about mods since i can never show pics but i've had 5 1/4" components in the dead pedal area of my '87 for a few years. the location is good for sound. no problems with highs, plus it lets you play with the equal pathlenths idea. this weekend i should finish some  pods in the same area for 8" 3 ways for my '86gt, and caught a sale on some 6 1/2" co-axials for a later fiero project, same spot. i also have them in the same spot in my chevy and my blazer (just tweeter amd small mid. the woofer's in the door).<P>i'm no fiberglass expert but a little (ok maybe a lot of) time, a gallon of resin and some fiberglass and you can put them where you want. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
